    "openrouter_cost_usd": 0.088852,
    "reply": "The retrieved records pair EGFR-directed clinical studies in non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) with ClinVar entries for EGFR sequence variants. The trials focus mainly on EGFR tyrosine kinase inhibitors [1]. The variant records are missense and synonymous changes annotated on the NM_005228.5 transcript [6]. The records do not state recruitment status, so none of these trials can be confirmed as currently recruiting.\n\n## EGFR-TKI Treatment Studies\n\nOne study retrospectively compares gefitinib, erlotinib and osimertinib in NSCLC [1: \"A Retrospective Study of EGFR-TKIs,Gefitinib, Erlotinib and Osimertinib in NSCLC Patients Treatment\"]. Another examines survival outcomes of EGFR-TKI therapy in advanced NSCLC carrying uncommon EGFR mutations [2: \"Survival Outcome of EGFR-TKI in Uncommon EGFR Mutant Advanced NSCLC\"]. A third evaluates osimertinib in advanced EGFR-positive disease [3: \"Osimertinib for Advanced EGFR-positive NSCLC Patients\"].\n\n## Leptomeningeal and Cellular Approaches\n\nOne study analyses cerebrospinal fluid in EGFR-mutant NSCLC with leptomeningeal disease [4: \"CSF Analysis in EGFR Mutant Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer With Leptomeningeal Disease\"]. Another tests EGFR/B7H3 CAR-T cells in lung cancer and triple-negative breast cancer [5: \"EGFR/B7H3 CAR-T on Lung Cancer and Triple Negative Breast Cancer\"].\n\n## ClinVar EGFR Variants\n\nClinVar:1000076 is NM_005228.5(EGFR):c.840C>A (p.Asn280Lys) [6]. ClinVar:1002380 is NM_005228.5(EGFR):c.2339T>C (p.Ile780Thr) [17]. ClinVar:1001782 is the synonymous variant NM_005228.5(EGFR):c.2619A>T (p.Gly873=) [16]. These records do not include clinical significance or any link to NSCLC.",
